xt-accent dark:text-dark-link" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 5.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 3h11A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 20 5.5v2A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 17.5 10h-11A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 7.5v-2ZM4 16a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 2.5-2.5h11A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 20 16v2a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-2.5 2.5h-11A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 18v-2Z"></path><path stroke-linecap="round" d="M7 6.5h.01M7 17h.01"></path></svg><dt class="mt-2.5 font-semibold text-ink dark:text-dark-foreground">11 origin regions</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[0.95rem] leading-snug text-slate-600 dark:text-dark-secondary">Files are fetched from origin machines across the Americas, Europe, Asia, and Australia.</dd></div><div class="p-4 border-b sm:border-b-0 lg:border-r border-hairline dark:border-dark-border"><svg class="w-6 h-6 text-accent dark:text-dark-link" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5"></circle><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m8.5 12.2 2.4 2.4 4.6-5"></path></svg><dt class="mt-2.5 font-semibold text-ink dark:text-dark-foreground">Verified bytes</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[0.95rem] leading-snug text-slate-600 dark:text-dark-secondary">Every file is digest-checked before it is cached, and corrupt entries heal themselves.</dd></div><div class="p-4"><svg class="w-6 h-6 text-accent dark:text-dark-link" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 3 5 5.8v5.4c0 4.3 2.9 7.4 7 9.3 4.1-1.9 7-5 7-9.3V5.8L12 3Z"></path><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m9.3 11.8 2 2 3.6-3.9"></path></svg><dt class="mt-2.5 font-semibold text-ink dark:text-dark-foreground">Supply-chain defense</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[0.95rem] leading-snug text-slate-600 dark:text-dark-secondary"><a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="https://shield.unpkg.com/">UNPKG Shield</a> pins or swaps compromised packages at the edge.</dd></div></dl><section id="quickstart"><h2 class="mt-20 mb-6 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-dark-foreground">Start in one line</h2><p>Point a script tag at a package file. Pin the full version in production so the response comes straight from the edge cache:</p><div class="mt-6"><div class="hljs-frame border border-hairline-strong dark:border-dark-border-strong bg-white dark:bg-dark-page"><div class="hljs-dark-listing p-4 font-mono text-sm leading-6 whitespace-pre overflow-x-auto" style="tab-size:2;"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">script</span> <span class="hljs-attr">src</span>=<span class="hljs-string">&quot;https://unpkg.com/preact@10.26.4/dist/preact.min.js&quot;</span>&gt;</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">script</span>&gt;</span></div></div></div><p class="mt-6">In a module, load the browser-ready build from <a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="https://esm.unpkg.com/">esm.unpkg.com</a>:</p><div class="mt-6"><div class="hljs-frame border border-hairline-strong dark:border-dark-border-strong bg-white dark:bg-dark-page"><div class="hljs-dark-listing p-4 font-mono text-sm leading-6 whitespace-pre overflow-x-auto" style="tab-size:2;"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">script</span> <span class="hljs-attr">type</span>=<span class="hljs-string">&quot;module&quot;</span>&gt;</span><span class="language-javascript">
  <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">React</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">&quot;https://esm.unpkg.com/react@18.3.1&quot;</span>;
</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">script</span>&gt;</span></div></div></div><p class="mt-6">Need to know what's inside a package first? Append <a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/guides/metadata-api"><code class="text-sm bg-paper-alt dark:bg-dark-panel">?meta</code></a> to any package URL for JSON metadata.</p></section><section id="ways-to-use"><h2 class="mt-20 mb-6 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-dark-foreground">Ways to use UNPKG</h2><ul class="ml-6 list-disc list-outside"><li class="marker:pr-2"><a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/guides/loading-files">Load files from npm</a>: any file, any package, one URL. Versions, entry points, and exports resolution explained.</li><li class="marker:pr-2 mt-2"><a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/guides/nobuild-apps">Build apps with no build step</a>: import maps turn a plain HTML file into a working app.</li><li class="marker:pr-2 mt-2"><a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/guides/browser-modules">Use native browser modules</a>: esm.unpkg.com converts packages into modules browsers load directly.</li><li class="marker:pr-2 mt-2"><a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/guides/inline-scripts">Run inline TypeScript and JSX</a>: the <code class="text-sm bg-paper-alt dark:bg-dark-panel">/run</code> helper transforms inline scripts in the page.</li><li class="mt-2"><a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/guides/metadata-api">Inspect packages programmatically</a>: file listings, sizes, and integrity hashes as JSON, for tools and agents.</li></ul><div class="mt-10" id="live-demo"><div class="hljs-frame border border-hairline-strong dark:border-dark-border-strong bg-white dark:bg-dark-page"><div class="hljs-dark-listing p-4 font-mono text-sm leading-6 white