</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">script</span>&gt;</span></div></div><div data-hydrate="{&quot;key&quot;:&quot;RunDemo&quot;,&quot;props&quot;:{&quot;runUrl&quot;:&quot;https://unpkg.com/run&quot;}}"><div class="mt-3 flex items-center gap-4"><button type="button" class="px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold border border-hairline-strong dark:border-dark-border-strong bg-paper-alt dark:bg-dark-panel hover:bg-slate-200 dark:hover:bg-dark-border cursor-pointer"><span class="grid"><span class="col-start-1 row-start-1 invisible" aria-hidden="true">Run this example</span><span class="col-start-1 row-start-1">Run this example</span></span></button><div hidden></div></div></div></div></section><section id="production"><h2 class="mt-20 mb-6 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-dark-foreground">Running in production</h2><p>Exact-version files are cached at the edge for a year, and every cached byte is digest-verified. A damaged entry is evicted and refetched, never served. If a version has to be withdrawn, it can be evicted from every cache layer without touching any other version. The <a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/network">network page</a> explains how, and the <a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/status">status page</a> describes how changes ship safely.</p><div class="mt-8 p-4 bg-paper-alt dark:bg-dark-panel"><p><span class="font-semibold">Serving production traffic through UNPKG?</span> <a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="https://shield.unpkg.com/" title="UNPKG Shield">UNPKG Shield</a> (currently in Beta) watches every npm release as it publishes. Arm a domain and a compromised version is pinned to the last known-good release (or blocked) at the edge, before a browser executes it. <a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/guides/supply-chain-security">How supply-chain defense works</a>.</p></div></section><section id="about"><h2 class="mt-20 mb-6 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-dark-foreground">Open source</h2><p>UNPKG is an <a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="https://github.com/unpkg" title="UNPKG on GitHub">open source project</a>, free to use, and not affiliated with npm. The <a class="inline-link text-accent dark:text-dark-link hover:underline" href="/guides">guides</a> go deeper on everything above.</p></section></main><div class="mt-24"><footer class="border-t border-hairline dark:border-dark-border text-slate-600 dark:text-dark-secondary"><div class="mx-auto lg:max-w-screen-md px-8 pt-10 pb-24 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-6"><div><p class="text-lg font-black text-ink dark:text-dark-foreground">UNPKG</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm">The CDN for everything on npm. Open source and free to use.</p><p class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-4"><a class="text-slate-600 dark:text-dark-foreground hover:text-slate-950 dark:hover:text-dark-foreground focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-slate-500 dark:focus-visible:outline-dark-muted" href="https://github.com/unpkg" title="UNPKG on GitHub" aria-label="UNPKG on GitHub"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="w-6 h-6"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12.006 2a9.847 9.847 0 0 0-6.484 2.44 10.32 10.32 0 0 0-3.393 6.17 10.48 10.48 0 0 0 1.317 6.955 10.045 10.045 0 0 0 5.4 4.418c.504.095.683-.223.683-.494 0-.245-.01-1.052-.014-1.908-2.78.62-3.366-1.21-3.366-1.21a2.711 2.711 0 0 0-1.11-1.5c-.907-.637.07-.621.07-.621.317.044.62.163.885.346.266.183.487.426.647.71.135.253.318.476.538.655a2.079 2.079 0 0 0 2.37.196c.045-.52.27-1.006.635-1.37-2.219-.259-4.554-1.138-4.554-5.07a4.022 4.022 0 0 1 1.031-2.75 3.77 3.77 0 0 1 .096-2.713s.839-.275 2.749 1.05a9.26 9.26 0 0 1 5.004 0c1.906-1.325 2.74-1.05 2.74-1.05.37.858.406 1.828.101 2.713a4.017 4.017 0 0 1 1.029